      "content": "{\"author\":{\"id\":\"U_kgDOBcQcsQ\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"alexandra5000\",\"name\":\"Aleksandra Spilkowska\"},\"body\":\"The [Histograms in delta temporality only](https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/opentelemetry/compatibility/limitations#histograms-in-delta-temporality-only) limitation in `docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md` is no longer accurate as a blanket statement.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nBoth delta and cumulative temporality are now supported for histograms and counters when sending data using the **ES OTLP endpoint** or **motlp** — on Elastic Stack 9.5+ and already on serverless. The relevant docs are at [Metric temporality](https://www.elastic.co/docs/manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint#metric-temporality).\\n\\nNote: cumulative temporality for histograms additionally requires `xpack.otel_data.histogram_field_type` set to `exponential_histogram` (which is the default on 9.4+).\\n\\n## Caveat\\n\\nThe **collector Elasticsearch exporter** does NOT support this yet — the limitation still applies when using that path. Work to add it is planned, but blocked on native exponential histogram support first.\\n\\n## Proposed doc change (lines 61–65)\\n\\n- Update the section title (no longer \\\"only delta\\\")\\n- Scope the remaining delta-only restriction to the ES exporter path\\n- Add a note pointing to the metric temporality docs for the OTLP endpoint path\\n- Add appropriate `applies_to` tags (stack: 9.5 / serverless for the lifted restriction)\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOMbWjGc8AAAABMnp19g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"github-actions\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"body\":\"<!-- docs-ai-menu:start -->\\n## Elastic Docs AI Menu\\n\\nCheck one box to run an AI workflow for this issue.\\n\\n- [ ] Triage ([`docs-triage`](https://github.com/elastic/docs-actions/blob/main/.github/workflows/oblt-aw-issue-triage.md)). Status: not started. <!-- docs-ai-menu:triage -->\\n- [ ] Scope the docs work ([`docs-issue-scope`](https://github.com/elastic/docs-actions/blob/main/.github/workflows/oblt-aw-docs-issue-scope.md)). Status: not started. <!-- docs-ai-menu:issue-scope -->\\n\\nPowered by GitHub Agentic Workflows and [docs-actions](https://github.com/elastic/docs-actions). For more information, reach out to the docs team.\\n\\n<!-- docs-ai-menu:end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-31T10:22:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/elastic/opentelemetry/issues/648#issuecomment-5141853686\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOMbWjGc8AAAAClLHBTg\",\"name\":\"Team:Ingest\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"ededed\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOMbWjGc8AAAACuv8s1A\",\"name\":\"docs-agent\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"aaaaaa\"}],\"number\":648,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Update histogram temporality limitation — now supported on OTLP endpoint (9.5+ / serverless)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/elastic/opentelemetry/issues/648\"}\n---\n648\n<shellId: 0 completed with exit code 0>"
