      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "toolu_013DGgCNDB7HQjwEYzNxcZYn",
      "content": "59. ## Metrics data ingestion\n60. \n61. ### Histogram and counter temporality\n62. \n63. ```{applies_to}\n64. stack: ga 9.5\n65. serverless: ga\n66. ```\n67. \n68. When you send data using the [{{es}} OTLP endpoint](docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality) (`motlp`), both `delta` and `cumulative` [temporality](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#temporality) are supported for histograms and counters. Refer to [Metric temporality](docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality) for details, including the requirement to set `xpack.otel_data.histogram_field_type` to `exponential_histogram` for cumulative histograms. This setting is the default from stack version 9.4.\n69. \n70. When you send data through the collector's {{es}} exporter, ingestion of OpenTelemetry metrics with the type [`Histogram`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#histogram) is only supported with `delta` temporality. Histograms with `cumulative` temporality are dropped before being ingested into {{es}}. Make sure to export histogram metrics with delta temporality or use the [`cumulativetodelta processor`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/processor/cumulativetodeltaprocessor) as a workaround to convert the temporality for histogram metrics.\n71. \n72. ### Exemplars\n73. \n74. Exemplars are discarded when ingesting metrics. Support for exemplars is planned for a future release.\n75. \n76. ## Limitations on managed Kubernetes environments\n77. \n78. Due to limitations with permissions on managed Kubernetes environments, such as GKE Autopilot or AWS Fargate, the default configurations and onboarding flows for {{edot}} don't fully work in those environments. This might result in decreased collection of data and certain observability views not showing that data."
